Parallel loop regression tests
==============================

  timeout 180 ./maxima-local --no-init --lisp=sbcl \
    --batch-string='run_testsuite(tests=[rtest_parallel_loop,rtest_parallel]);'

Use each configured Lisp and require "No unexpected errors" in the log;
Maxima can continue after a Lisp error and still exit with status zero.

The 30 examples include exact and floating bounds, empty and descending
ranges, control evaluation order and side effects, cleanup after errors,
the serial fallback, nested loops and a floating step which stops making
progress. The complete suite includes this file automatically.

parallel-loop-check.lisp supplies a body which records values under a
lock, then sorts them after all workers have joined. Iteration order is
intentionally unspecified; the multiset of values must be correct. A
private deterministic LCG produces 192 short ranges with signed steps,
large integers, and rational limits extremely close to a step boundary.
Expected values are calculated independently in exact Common Lisp
arithmetic. The same cases run through the ordinary evaluator, parallel
evaluation and the forced one-core fallback. Test collection does not
modify Maxima's random state or share its accumulator between jobs.
